{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"76520c18d55160c8","name":"card_event_mountain_offense","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/WinterWar/events/card_event_mountain_offense","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"MOUNTAIN OFFENSIVE","text":"Add a random 1-cost, 2-cost and 3-cost unit with Alpine to your support line.","flavorText":"In July 1942 Germany launched Operation Edelweiss, named after the mountain flower, which was an offensive into the mountainous region of Caucasus in the Soviet Union. The ensuing Battle of Caucasus lasted from 1942 to 1944 and involved intense combat in the rugged and challenging terrain of the Caucasus Mountains. The primary German objective was to secure the oil-rich regions in the area, particularly the Baku oil fields. German forces, including mountain troops and other divisions, faced not only the harsh natural conditions but also fierce resistance from Soviet forces. Despite initial gains, the Germans ultimately faced setbacks and by 1943 they started to withdraw from the region. However, it wasn’t until 1944 that the Soviet forces managed to get full control of the Caucasus.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":6,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_mountain_offense","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_mountain_offense_title","SourceString":"MOUNTAIN OFFENSIVE","LocalizedString":"MOUNTAIN OFFENSIVE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_mountain_offense_text","SourceString":"Add a random 1-cost, 2-cost and 3-cost unit with Alpine to your support line.","LocalizedString":"Add a random 1-cost, 2-cost and 3-cost unit with Alpine to your support line."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_mountain_offense_history","SourceString":"In July 1942 Germany launched Operation Edelweiss, named after the mountain flower, which was an offensive into the mountainous region of Caucasus in the Soviet Union. The ensuing Battle of Caucasus lasted from 1942 to 1944 and involved intense combat in the rugged and challenging terrain of the Caucasus Mountains. The primary German objective was to secure the oil-rich regions in the area, particularly the Baku oil fields. German forces, including mountain troops and other divisions, faced not only the harsh natural conditions but also fierce resistance from Soviet forces. Despite initial gains, the Germans ultimately faced setbacks and by 1943 they started to withdraw from the region. However, it wasn’t until 1944 that the Soviet forces managed to get full control of the Caucasus.","LocalizedString":"In July 1942 Germany launched Operation Edelweiss, named after the mountain flower, which was an offensive into the mountainous region of Caucasus in the Soviet Union. The ensuing Battle of Caucasus lasted from 1942 to 1944 and involved intense combat in the rugged and challenging terrain of the Caucasus Mountains. The primary German objective was to secure the oil-rich regions in the area, particularly the Baku oil fields. German forces, including mountain troops and other divisions, faced not only the harsh natural conditions but also fierce resistance from Soviet forces. Despite initial gains, the Germans ultimately faced setbacks and by 1943 they started to withdraw from the region. However, it wasn’t until 1944 that the Soviet forces managed to get full control of the Caucasus."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/CandidateArtwork/Winter_War/t_mountain_offensive_vs_2.t_mountain_offensive_vs_2","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":